# Keep the build context small and, above all, free of secrets.
#
# `.env` is the important line here: it is the one file in the repository
# that is expected to hold a real Atlas connection string, and a build
# context is copied into the daemon whether or not a COPY references it.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.github

.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

tests
eval
scripts
docs
*.md
!README.md

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
